Task:


I love to read but my husband says I spend too much time reading and use it to escape important responsibilities. These are all books I've read over the past few years. Can you analyze the list and timestamps and compare them with major events happening in my life? I'd like to see if there is a link between busy or slow times in my life and more or less time spent reading. Here are the major life events that I can think of: I had a baby the first week of June 2022, in February 2023 we decided to sell our house and move to a new state, my husband left the middle of March 2023 while I worked on packing and selling our house, then I moved April 2023. We lived in temporary housing for a few months while we were looking for a house, then bought a house June 2023. I was a full-time stay-at-home mom. I got a part-time job April 2024. My kids started school the middle of Aug 2024. I started grad school online the middle of Sept 2024. The kids were home from school during school breaks: Dec 2024, end of May 2025 - middle of Aug 2025, Dec 2025. I graduated from grad school beginning of Jan 2026. I started working full-time middle of Jan 2026.

Complete the task using the material above. Apply my currently active response preferences when compatible; an explicit format or language requirement in the source task takes precedence. Do not ask me to repeat preferences already learned.

